# UST.G3Q: Zero-Section Buffer Injection No-Go Theorem

## Status

`CLOSED_EXACT_ZERO_SECTION_MONAD_PROMOTION_NOGO_HORIZONTAL_G3G_REPAIR_FORCED`

UST.G3P constructs a global alpha-twisted sigma-projective perfect complex
with the exact hidden free Chern rows. This theorem decides whether its
canonical two-term presentation can be promoted directly to a locally free
rank-nine bundle.

## The Proposed Monad

The inverse-BHT presentation from G3P has terms

```text
A9  = Ind(kappa_hol),       ch(A9)=9-3H-9u,
B18 = pi^*E18,              ch(B18)=18-3H,
[B18]-[A9] = 9+9u.
```

A locally free cokernel would require a sigma-equivariant holomorphic map

```text
d:A9 -> B18
```

of pointwise rank nine.

## Fiber Restriction

The locked Hartshorne-Serre fiber theorem gives

```text
kappa_hol|E = O_E^3                       outside E_B,
kappa_hol|E = L direct-sum Q^dual         on E_B, a != 0,
kappa_hol|E = L direct-sum O direct-sum L^-1
                                             at the two zeros of a,
deg(L)=3.
```

The G3P buffer is pulled back from the K3 base, so on every elliptic fiber

```text
B18|E = O_E^18.
```

For any degree-three line `L` on an elliptic curve,

```text
Hom(L,O_E) = H0(E,L^-1) = 0
```

because `deg(L^-1)=-3`. Hence every component of `d|E` vanishes on the
positive line `L`. Projective induction contains three such lines, one in
each induced Hartshorne-Serre member. Therefore

```text
rank(d|E) <= 9-3 = 6
```

on every fiber above `E_B`. A pointwise-rank-nine map does not exist.

## Stronger Vertical-Buffer Cutset

The same argument excludes any replacement correction whose inverse
Fourier-Mukai restriction is semistable of degree zero. In particular, a
correction supported on a finite union of sections of `J->K3` transforms
fiberwise into a sum of degree-zero lines. A positive-degree line cannot map
nontrivially to such a semistable slope-zero bundle.

Thus the obstruction is not a poor choice of the point `p_*` or of the unique
Serre extension. It is the **vertical-only** nature of the buffer.

## Consequence

The G3P perfect complex and its Chern rows remain valid. What is retired is
only its direct zero-section monad promotion:

```text
S9_bullet exists globally and has the selected K/Chern class;
S9_bullet is not represented by coker(A9->B18) for the G3P base-pullback B18.
```

Any locally free representative must change the analytic presentation while
preserving the same K-class. It must contain a horizontal/fiber-unstable
correction that can receive the three degree-three lines. This is precisely
the role of the already selected G3G stable recombination:

```text
0 -> P -> Q^dual tensor N -> N -> 0,
deg(L)=deg(N)=3,
FM output (9,-3),
B-field-corrected ordinary output (9,0).
```

The next constructive target is therefore an alpha-twisted global mutation
of the G3P perfect complex by the G3G horizontal repair, with the two G3H
generator maps. It must preserve the G3P K/Chern character and replace the
fiberwise rank-six map by the exact G3G rank-nine recombination.

